.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
# Build artefacts created by `uv tool install` / `pip install` / `uv build`.
# Regenerated on every install, never committed.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
._*
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
# mcpbrain/google_oauth_client.json is the tenant's OAuth desktop client. It is
# NOT committed: this repo is PUBLIC (it was described here as private, which had
# stopped being true), and the client is the one genuinely private part of a
# tenant profile. It lives in the private mcpbrain-tenant repo and is copied in by
# `python bin/tenant.py use ../mcpbrain-tenant`, which bin/release.py requires
# before it will build. mcpbrain/tenant.json holds no secrets and IS committed.
mcpbrain/google_oauth_client.json

# The curated gold eval sets are TENANT DATA, not product. They held real
# Centrepoint content in this PUBLIC repo — named staff tied to employment
# agreements, an EOY review, WWCC/Safer-Churches training status — and the
# tenant-literal guard could never catch it, because the spec deliberately
# excludes tests/ as "fixtures and history". Their chunk ids point into one
# organisation's own store, so a fork cannot use another's anyway. They live in
# the private mcpbrain-tenant repo and are copied in by
# `python bin/tenant.py use ../mcpbrain-tenant`. Absent, load_gold_cases()
# returns [] and the gold floor test skips honestly.
tests/eval/golden_retrieval_set.yaml
tests/eval/golden_retrieval_set_mcpbrain_candidate.yaml

# tenant_people.json is a PERSON-name analogue of the gold-set problem above: a
# real staff surname ("Okafor") sat in this PUBLIC repo's tests/ for months
# because the tenant-literal guard only ever checked org/infrastructure
# identifiers, never staff names, and tests/ wasn't even scanned. A guard file
# that enumerates real names to check for their own absence would just
# reintroduce the leak it exists to prevent, so the forbidden-names list itself
# is tenant data: a JSON list of surnames/full names, kept in the private
# mcpbrain-tenant repo and copied in by `python bin/tenant.py use
# ../mcpbrain-tenant`. Absent, the person-name check in
# test_no_tenant_literals.py skips honestly.
mcpbrain/tenant_people.json
google_token.json
google_account
client_secret.json

# Per-user local state from the Claude Code "remember" skill — session
# transcripts, log lines, scratch files. Not part of the shipped repo.
.remember/

# Daemon runtime artefacts that may land beside the data dir if MCPBRAIN_HOME
# is ever pointed at the repo (it shouldn't be, but ignore defensively).
control_port
control_token
daemon.lock
*.mcpbrain.log
*.mcpbrain.err
enrich_queue/
enrich_inbox/
